== Abstract ==

This document specifies trusted-dealer generation and verification of threshold key material for the FROST signing protocol in [https://github.com/siv2r/bip-frost-signing BIP 445]. It specializes the Shamir secret-sharing and Feldman verifiable secret-sharing construction in [https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9591#appendix-C RFC 9591 Appendix C] for secp256k1, defining participant identifiers, encodings, a key-generation tweak, share verification, and acceptance requirements.

A dealer generates or imports an initial secret, distributes one secret share to each participant, and publishes commitments from which participants derive the threshold public key and public shares. The dealer learns the complete secret and must be trusted to protect and erase secret material. Signing and distributed key generation are outside the scope of this proposal.

